## API Reference

### AuthService (Singleton)

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `initialize()` | Load persisted tokens from secure storage |
| `setTokens(accessToken, refreshToken, expiresIn, userData)` | Store new token set |
| `updateAccessToken(accessToken, expiresIn)` | Update only access token |
| `refreshAccessToken(endpoint, clientId, clientSecret)` | Refresh access token using refresh token |
| `clearTokens()` | Remove all tokens from storage |
| `logout(revokeEndpoint, clientId, clientSecret)` | Revoke server-side token then clear local |
| `handleAuthCallback(url, config)` | Exchange authorization code for tokens |
| `subscribe(listener)` | Subscribe to auth state changes |
| `getAuthState()` | Get current auth state snapshot |
| `isAuthenticated()` | Check if user has valid tokens |
| `isTokenExpired()` | Check if access token is expired |

### AuthProvider Props

| Prop | Type | Required | Description |
|------|------|----------|-------------|
| `config` | Object | Yes | OAuth/OIDC configuration |
| `config.authEndpoint` | string | For OAuth | Authorization endpoint URL |
| `config.tokenEndpoint` | string | Yes | Token endpoint URL |
| `config.revokeEndpoint` | string | No | Token revocation endpoint |
| `config.clientId` | string | Yes | OAuth client ID |
| `config.clientSecret` | string | No | OAuth client secret |
| `config.redirectUri` | string | For OAuth | Redirect URI for auth code flow |
| `config.scopes` | string[] | No | Requested scopes (default: openid profile email offline_access) |

### useAuth Return Value

| Property | Type | Description |
|----------|------|-------------|
| `isAuthenticated` | boolean | Current authentication status |
| `isLoading` | boolean | Initialization/loading state |
| `accessToken` | string\|null | Current access token |
| `refreshToken` | string\|null | Current refresh token |
| `user` | object\|null | User profile data |
| `isTokenExpired` | boolean | Whether access token is expired |
| `login(credentials?)` | Function | Login via password or OAuth |
| `register(userData)` | Function | Register new user |
| `logout()` | Function | Logout and revoke tokens |
| `refreshToken()` | Function | Manually trigger token refresh |
| `updateUser(data)` | Function | Update local user data |

### useAuthFetch

Returns an `authFetch(url, options)` function that:
- Automatically attaches Bearer token
- Refreshes expired tokens before request
- Retries once on 401 with fresh token
- Logs out on refresh failure

## Security Considerations

1. **Refresh Token Rotation**: Server should issue new refresh token on each refresh (supported automatically)
2. **Token Revocation**: Call `logout()` with revoke endpoint to invalidate server-side tokens
3. **Secure Storage**: Keychain/Keystore with `WHEN_UNLOCKED_THIS_DEVICE_ONLY` prevents backup extraction
4. **PKCE Support**: Use `code_verifier` in `handleAuthCallback` config for public clients
5. **Short Access Token Lifetime**: Keep access tokens short-lived (5-15 min), refresh tokens longer (days/weeks)

## Platform Notes

| Platform | Storage Mechanism | Security Level |
|----------|-------------------|----------------|
| iOS | Keychain (kSecAttrAccessibleWhenUnlockedThisDeviceOnly) | Hardware-backed |
| Android | Keystore / EncryptedSharedPreferences | Hardware-backed (API 23+) |
| Web / Other | AsyncStorage (unencrypted) | Software-only |

